    files: list = dataclasses.field(default_factory=list)
@

The errors that [[canvaslms]] should report, rather than crash on, are
those of a remote service that failed or changed: a launch that broke, a
request that failed, a name FBF no longer has, a kind of data we cannot
read.
They are nearly the errors that our own commands report as messages
(\cref{CLI}), but not quite.
A command reports any [[LookupError]] and [[OSError]], which in a view
would also hide a [[KeyError]] of a bug or a file we failed to write, and
show it as FBF's failure.
So we take FBF's own lookup error, the unknown kind of data, and of the
[[OSError]]s only those of [[requests]], which the downloads below raise.
Any other exception is a bug, here or in the caller, and must stay loud.
The [[Viewer]] below carries them too, as [[errors]], since a caller that
found the class through the import system holds the viewer, not the module.

