\section{The grade}
\label{ViewGrade}

The grade breakdown is that of [[fbf progress]] (\cref{Progress}) for one
student.
We cannot call [[assignment_progress]], which builds the rows of all
students, fetches the Canvas scores of all and reports on all of them on
standard error; we take its parts instead.
Of the student's progresses we take the one that explains the grade, by
the same [[preference]], and the grade sent is fetched for that one only.
The Canvas score is the submission's own, which [[canvaslms]] already has.

<<constants>>=
GRADE_TITLE = "FeedbackFruits grade"
<<functions>>=
def grade_section(activity, users, assignment, student, score, mine=None):
    """Return the `Section` of the grade breakdown of `users`.

    `mine`, if given, are the progresses of `users`, fetched before.
    """
    if mine is None:
        mine = [progress for progress in activity.progresses
                if related_id(progress, "actor") in users]
    if not mine:
        return Section(GRADE_TITLE, "No progress in FeedbackFruits.")
    progress = max(mine, key=progress_module.preference)
    row = progress_module.progress_row(
        assignment, progress, activity.tasks,
        progress_module.sent_grades(activity.fbf, [progress]),
        student, {student.id: score})
    return Section(GRADE_TITLE, grade_text(row))
@

The text gives the totals first and then the facets, the parts that FBF
adds up to the total, with the points earned of the points possible.
FBF's overall grade is a percentage (\cref{Progress}); we show it beside
the score in Canvas's points, since the two may differ and the difference
is what a teacher looks for.

<<functions>>=
def grade_text(row):
    """Return the Markdown of a `Progress` row."""
    number = progress_module.number
    lines = [f"- Overall: {number(row.overall)} %, "
             f"{number(row.fbf_score)} of {number(row.points_possible)} "
             "points",
             f"- In Canvas: {number(row.canvas_score)} points",
             f"- Published by FeedbackFruits: "
             f"{'yes' if row.published else 'no'}"]
    if row.sent_grade is not None:
        lines.append(f"- Sent to Canvas: {row.sent_grade} ({row.sent_status})")
    facets = [f"- {facet.task_type} {facet.task_order}: "
              f"{progress_module.facet_text(facet)}"
              for facet in row.facets if facet.weight]
    return "\n".join(lines + ([""] + facets if facets else []))
